{"id":"v6","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":6,"of":8,"title":"The two passives","titleHe":"פֻּעַל וְהֻפְעַל","goal":"Recognise pu'al and huf'al on the page.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Two binyanim exist only as passives: פֻּעַל is the passive of pi'el, הֻפְעַל the passive of hif'il. Neither has an infinitive or an imperative, and outside the third person they're rare — so this is a recognition lesson, not a production one."},{"type":"passives","items":[{"id":"pual","he":"פֻּעַל","en":"pu'al","of":"piel","note":"The passive of pi'el — something is being done to the subject.","verb":{"root":"ד־ב־ר","en":"to be spoken (of)"},"present":{"ms":"מְדֻבָּר","fs":"מְדֻבֶּרֶת","mp":"מְדֻבָּרִים","fp":"מְדֻבָּרוֹת"},"past":{"3ms":"דֻּבַּר","3fs":"דֻּבְּרָה","3p":"דֻּבְּרוּ"},"future":{"3ms":"יְדֻבַּר","3fs":"תְּדֻבַּר","3p":"יְדֻבְּרוּ"}},{"id":"hufal","he":"הֻפְעַל","en":"huf'al","of":"hifil","note":"The passive of hif'il.","verb":{"root":"ס־ב־ר","en":"to be explained"},"present":{"ms":"מֻסְבָּר","fs":"מֻסְבֶּרֶת","mp":"מֻסְבָּרִים","fp":"מֻסְבָּרוֹת"},"past":{"3ms":"הֻסְבַּר","3fs":"הֻסְבְּרָה","3p":"הֻסְבְּרוּ"},"future":{"3ms":"יֻסְבַּר","3fs":"תֻּסְבַּר","3p":"יֻסְבְּרוּ"}}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Look for the u vowel where you'd expect a or i. מְדַבֵּר speaks becomes מְדֻבָּר is spoken of; מַסְבִּיר explains becomes מֻסְבָּר is explained."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מְדֻבָּר","en":"spoken of, in question","translit":"meduba r"},{"he":"מֻסְבָּר","en":"explained","translit":"musbar"},{"he":"מְקֻבָּל","en":"accepted, customary","translit":"mekubal"},{"he":"מֻכָּן","en":"ready, prepared","translit":"muchan"},{"he":"מְסֻדָּר","en":"arranged, tidy","translit":"mesudar"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["king","spoken of, in question","looks at","very"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מְדֻבָּר","translit":"meduba r"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["come! (f.)","explained","small","to eat"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מֻסְבָּר","translit":"musbar"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["accepted, customary","tree","gets dressed","sea"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מְקֻבָּל","translit":"mekubal"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["ready, prepared","yes","because","seems, looks"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מֻכָּן","translit":"muchan"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["looks at","arranged, tidy","was born","for example"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מְסֻדָּר","translit":"mesudar"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “arranged, tidy”?","options":["בָּא","מְסֻדָּר","אַל","אוֹתוֹ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “accepted, customary”?","options":["מְקֻבָּל","מָחָר","נִמְצָא","מַהֵר"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “explained”?","options":["אָמַר","מְקַבֵּל","שֶׁל","מֻסְבָּר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"מְקֻבָּל","translit":"mekubal","en":"accepted, customary"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["מֻסְבָּר","explained"],["מֻכָּן","ready, prepared"],["מְסֻדָּר","arranged, tidy"],["מְקֻבָּל","accepted, customary"],["מְדֻבָּר","spoken of, in question"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “ready, prepared”?","options":["מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ","אַחַר כָּךְ","אִתִּי","מֻכָּן"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מְדֻבָּר","מֻכָּן","מְקֻבָּל","מֻסְבָּר"],"correct":3,"say":"מֻסְבָּר","he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “ready, prepared” in Hebrew","answer":"מֻכָּן","hint":"muchan"}]}